WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.860
[Mark]: Hello, everybody! My name is Markiplier,

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.820
and welcome back to Job Simulator.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.900
We're gonna go with the store clerk.
[Job Bot]: Are you a fan of slushies and hot dogs?

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.060
[Job Bot]: You'll love the convenience store!

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:09.080
[Mark]: Yay!

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.800
I don't know how to do that, but

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.800
Wade used to work at a UDF in Cincinnati,

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.220
and if you don't know what a UDF is,

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.520
it's basically like a dairy store.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.860
Hello!

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.080
Hi.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.320
Ooh, why do I want to put... Hello?

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.200
[Job Bot]: Welcome to an accurate simulation of

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.740
[Job Bot]: CONVENIENCE  STORE CLERK.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:25.080
[Mark]: Uh, okay?

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.120
[Job Bot]: Take a look at this board for instructions,

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.360
and grab a ticket when you're ready to get started.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.300
[Mark]: God dammit, why is everything on a ticket-based system? You know, people could just walk up

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.900
and ask me, and then I would... like, begrudgingly help them.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.080
And the only thing related to this that I did was working at *ding* Kroger's,

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.600
in the non-food stocking section!

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.080
I was a non-food stocking clerk!

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.940
And that basically meant I just stood at the

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:48.760
jewelry and perfume counter and...

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.340
stocked the adult diapers!

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.100
That's what I did!

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.120
Boopity-boopity-boop, bing-bIng! Okay, hello.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.100
There's no one here, though.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.440
[Job Bot]: You can start by cleaning off your counter!

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.920
[Mark]:Ehhowiuaaguuuguueuaughuhguaugauauh

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:03.940
What do I do?!

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:04.800
Get out of here!

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.080
I don't know if I'm supposed to do this!

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.080
Ah, these seem like important things.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.780
Okay.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.780
Oh, probably in the trash. Now that would have been--

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:11.700
yeah, that would have been smart.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.440
[Job Bot]: Turn on the security camera so you can keep an eye on the store.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.560
[Mark]: Boink! Okay. Ooh...

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:24.720
Wait, where am I?! Oh God! I'm not real! I'm fake!

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.260
Oh, my life is a lie!

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:31.120
[Job Bot]: All righty. Let's get to business! Here's your first customer.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:34.300
[Mark]: Hello! Don't steal anything. I'm watching you!

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.260
Everyone's a criminal until proven otherwise!

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:38.860
[Lady Bot]: Good afternoon, human. I would like to purchase these...

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:39.640
[Lady Bot]: CHIPS.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.240
[in-game crunching noise]
[Mark]: Oh!

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.360
[More in-game crunching]

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.160
[In-game crunching continues]
[Mark]: Wow! [laughs] I found an exploit!

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.040
UAG UAG
Ok.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.080
Boop!

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.320
Yay! It's all the joy of doing this.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.160
Here you go! Ooh, shit.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.180
Here you go! That'll be--

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.720
[Lady Bot]: Can I also get one of those meat cylinders, please?

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.440
[Mark]: Where do I, excuse me?!

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.360
[Job Bot]: Hotdogs are in the freezer.
[Mark]: Oh.
[Job Bot]: Make sure you heat them up,

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.440
at least a little bit.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.560
[Mark]: Okay! All right, here we go.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.340
Oh, God! Ugh!

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.020
There you go! I don't wanna heat it--

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.500
Whoop, never mind then. She was pissed about that.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.100
Bloink! Oh, okay! Here we go.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.300
I get these on the rollers there. If I know anything about convenience stores, because I used to eat

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:27.060
a lot of this type of food back in Cincinnati, when I was UNbelieeeevably poor! Like--

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.820
[Lady Bot]: Mmm, that looks... ACCEPTABLE.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:32.300
[Lady Bot]: Hurry up and scan that, so I can get eating already.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:37.420
[Mark]: Uh, I don't know how this is gonna work, Madame, but I'm just gonna put faith in the system!

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.480
HEAPA!
Oh, wow, it worked! Boink!

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.560
[Lady Bot]: You can just hand that hot dog to me, human. Thanks a bunch!

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.560
[Mark]: You're welcome. I'll take money now!

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.120
[Job Bot]: To finalize a sale, pull the lever on the register.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:48.500
[Mark]: Kerchunkles!

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:51.140
[Lady Bot]: All righty! Here's your paper currency.
[Mark]: Oh, you had a-- Oh.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.860
Wha--uh-- Gah.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:03:00.080
Okay! You're dumb! We're doing it! We're cooperating!

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.700
[Mark quietly cries to self]

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:02.900
There you go.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:06.760
[Lady Bot]: Many thanks! Have a PROFITABLE day!

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:10.900
[Mark]: Hey! Profit! Okay. Did I do good, boss?

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.860
Did I do good? I don't know what I'm doing.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:17.000
[Job Bot]: It was important for stores like this to maintain a constant stream of customers,

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:21.680
so the cashiers wouldn't have time to contemplate their rapidly approaching obsolescence.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.840
[Mark]: Okay, then. That's a little unnecessary.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:26.840
Boink! Boink. Boink! Boink.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.840
[Classy Bot]: Will you kind-- Ah, yes, much better!

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.680
[Mark]: Haha, give me money! Now!

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.680
[Classy Bot]: I'll take one of those frozen slushy delights!

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.880
[Mark]: Wh--sh-- Fuck you. Okay.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:39.300
Frozen slushy delights. I like to mix n' match!

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.300
I don't know about you guys at home, but it's my baby.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.800
[Classy Bot]: Would you be able to jumbo-size that?

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:48.160
[Mark, mockingly]: How do I jumbo-size this? How do I do that?

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.500
Here you go! Boink!

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.360
Have a good day! Oh, I can maximi-- Ohh!

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.700
Oh, my God! Oh! Whoa!!!!!

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.380
[Classy Bot]: I love the taste of sugar!
[Mark]: [miming gulping down the drink]

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.380
Okay, I'm gonna need to get you some more, because--

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:05.380
Battery acid blue! Thermal paste pink!

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:08.120
I actually imagine that I would enjoy battery acid blue,

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.080
because I love all types of blue drinks.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.640
[Classy Bot]: You are very good at scanning! Now, would you pass that to me?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.020
[Mark]: You got it, buddy! I didn't know if I--

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.980
[Classy Bot]: And here's some bank notes for you!
[Mark]: Okay.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.700
[Classy Bot]: Keep the change, good human!

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:23.920
[Mark]: Keep the change? What? Fuck off! I don't need your charity!

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:29.000
What do you want?!
[Elderly Bot]: I'll take a paper copy of yesterday's news.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.420
[Mark, in a faux posh accent]: Uh, okay! Well, then. If you want yesterday's news,

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:39.580
we've got a lot of that. No one read it then; no one reads it now. Anything else?

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:42.640
[Elderly Bot]: I'll take my daily lottery ticket, as well.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:48.040
[Mark, loudly]: Oh, lottery tickets, eh? Well, I've got just the thing for you. Oh!

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:49.960
If I could only get it...

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.800
Is this made by the same people that made "aaaAAH the falling game"?

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:00.380
[Elderly Bot]: Oh, dear, I'm feeling a little faint today, dearie.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:03.980
[Mark]: (Unintelligible mocking noises)
[Elderly Bot]: Do you think you could scratch that lottery ticket for me?

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:06.880
[Mark]: Oh, you got it!
[Elderly Bot]: You can use my quarter.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:09.600
[Mark]: What if I win it? [soft groan]

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:14.920
[Still poor Bot]: Oh. I guess I won't be getting those upgrades today.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:20.420
[Mark]: No, you won't, so shut up about your sad life! I'm a store clerk!

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.660
[Elderly Bot]: Let me just write you a check for those.
[Mark]: Oh, God.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:23.800
[Elderly Bot]: There we are.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:29.000
[Mark]: [groan of frustration] Oh, I guess it works. Oh, all right, then.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:34.280
[Elderly Bot]: Oh, what a kind young human you are. Have a lovely day!

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:38.720
[Mark]: Ah, go fuck yourself. I don't care. Eat a diiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiick!

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:43.460
[Business Bot]: So I'm, like, "Yeah, brah, it's a buyers' market." They're looking at me like I'm crazy. You know.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:47.380
And what.. what are you talki-- no, No! I'm talking to you, no.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:50.700
You! Yeah, you! You got that hot dog all ready?

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.700
[Mark]: Uh, sure?

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:58.380
[Business Bot won't shut the fricking heck up]

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:03.720
[Business Bot]: I want some gum. No, not you. The human. I want to buy some gum already!

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:04.880
[Mark]: Okay.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.880
[Business Bot]: What is this, your first job?

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:11.220
[Mark]: Yes! It is! I've never worked before! Humans don't work!

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:15.160
[Business Bot]: No, not you. The other...uh...  Forget it.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:19.980
[Mark, annoyed]: Okay, I guess you're done now! Go away, please! Boopity-boopity-boopity boop!

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:24.360
[Business Bot]: Am I right? Yeah. No, you! No... I'm talkin' to you, bro!

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.700
[Mark]: Who? Me? I... The money didn't go through!

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:32.140
[Job Bot]: No matter how irritating the customer, humans will require to smile and be polite.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:36.320
[Mark]: You don't know how humans work if you think that's how the real world was!

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:40.200
You think we HAVE to?! Oh, you sweet summer child!

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:43.680
[Mark]
Aww! It's so cute. Look! It's you!

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:48.040
[Mom Bot]: Put that nice healthy banana up there for the human.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.660
[Mark, imitating Mom Bot]: Oh, a nice healthy banana! I've seen healthier things.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:51.800
You don't even know about healthy!

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:56.860
[Mom Bot]: Stay here for a minute, dearie. Mommy needs to use the little bots' room.

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.860
[Mark]: You're not a "little bot." Shut up.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:02.700
[Child Bot]: Sugar. SUGAR. SUGAR! Gimme sugar!

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:03.900
[Mark]: Okay, there you go.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.900
[Child Bot]: Yummy! More! More!

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:11.300
[Mark]: I--I only have so much sugar... Ooh! I know just the thing for distracting annoying little girls.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:21.500
It's gonna be SUUUUUUPER-SIZED! SUUUUUUUPER...SIZED. Boink. There you go.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.500
Man, that technology, huh? Boink!

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.220
[Child Bot]: Yummy! More!

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:28.440
[Mark]: More?! You greedy little girl! What more do you want? Here's a Twinkie

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:30.440
that's probably a thousand years old.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:35.440
Have fuuuun...with your diabetes... Ketchup, too.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:38.400
[Mom Bot]: All right, then. Sorry about the wait. Have you rung up our order!

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:42.320
[Mark]: Oh, yeah. It's amazingly expensive, surprisingly.(1.000.000)

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:44.880
[Mom Bot] : Dearie, can you hand the human the money?

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:48.620
[Mark]: Give me the money!
[Child Bot]: Whoa, money? Okay, here. [laughing]

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:52.200
[Mom Bot]: What did you do to my darling?! Come back here!

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.900
[Mark]: Well, I didn't do anything! what are you accusing me of?!

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:58.720
And why is she in charge of your money? What kind of adult parent are you?

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:04.460
[Job Bot]: Just do whatever the customer - or their children - wants. And make sure you always grab that money.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:09.500
[Mark]: I got the money. Don't worry about that, Job Bot. Do you robots even care about money?

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.960
[Energy Bot]: Yo! This place is lookin' sick!
[Mark]: YEA, BRO!

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:16.500
[Energy Bot]: You know what it needs? More "Maximum Energy" branding. 
[Mark]: [UAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAG

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:19.800
[energetically angry] I completely agree, bro! You know what's gonna crank this up, bro?!

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:26.880
[normally] Sorry, I needed to tone down the energy just a little bit. Okay.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:34.040
[repeated scanning beeping]: Okay, that one's good. And then this, too?

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:44.160
Okay, got it! Wait. Uh, wait.
There we go! You're all good, buddy! Ring that up...

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.800
What else do you-- What the hell is this? Stacking?

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:51.040
What? What is this? What is that?! I don't know what that is!

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:54.720
[Energy Bot]: Yeah, that's the one! Let's max this thing out!

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.500
[Mark]: Wait, what are you talking about?

00:08:56.500 --> 00:09:00.640
[Energy Bot]: I have to go to the bathroom, so I'm counting on you to really push the envelope on this thing.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:04.040
[Mark]: Bigger!
[Energy Bot]: If you're all done, just hit that button,

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:05.180
and let's lock this thing in!

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:09.720
[Mark]: Okay! What?! What'd I do?!

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:14.140
[Energy Bot, furtively]: Psst. Hey. Human. Over here!

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:19.120
Uh... I need something for, uh...cleaning?

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:23.860
[Mark]: There you go. Have fun! I know what you got!
[Energy Bot]: I guess I can make this work?

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:25.640
I'll be out in a second.

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:29.940
[Mark]: Wait, how do you understand the concept of us wiping our own asses,

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:33.040
and yet you can't understand the concept of what's going on in basic human instinct?

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:34.260
[Energy Bot]: All right, much better. Now let's see this display, human!

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:38.180
All right, lookin' good!
[Mark]: Uh...

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:43.980
[Energy Bot] And now, we're on brand, baby! Boom! Haha. Peace out, human.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:48.820
[Mark]: Okay, peace out, bruh. Have a good one. You didn't pay for it,

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:52.340
Even though I didn't... I was told to always grab the money!

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:56.220
That was like, number one lesson, boss!
Hello, how are you doing?

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:58.780
[Athletic Bot]: Oh-ho, I just got back from jogging and...

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:02.960
Oh, man, do you have something to replenish my electrolytes?

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:08.680
[Mark]: I sure do! I don't know what the hell this is, but it... It's Electric Blue Goo!

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:12.320
I love Electric Blue Goo! It's got what plants crave!

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:16.140
Oh, shit. Well, you know what? No one ever liked Electric Blue Goo.

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:19.800
People do like Mountain Scream! It's got what plants crave! (Again)

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:22.160
...Shit.

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:25.620
Well, I may have fucked that one up. Okay.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:31.020
I always like Sweet Generic Off Brand Cola! It's got what plants crave! (...again)

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:36.420
Ah, shit! You didn't want any of this!
Where am I supposed to get that?!

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:40.560
Oh, in here. Why do I have it in here?
[Mark babbles softly to himself]

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.460
How about you get extra big jumbo one?
[Athletic Bot]: Oh! This, uh...

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:46.440
This Maximum Energy stuff? Uh, looks new! Right?

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:51.020
Uh.... It looks like you have to shake it? Can you shake it?

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:54.980
[Mark, in disbelief]: I did shake it! I already shaked it! I shooked it! Gimme your money!

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:58.460
Stop talkin' about me how to do my job! [nice English, Mark]

00:10:58.460 --> 00:10:59.560
Take it! Take it! Thank you.

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:04.900
[annoyedly]: Now leave.
[Energetic Bot]: You got your money now! Gimme the drink!

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:11.180
[Energy Bot gulps the drink] Oh! Whoa! I feel energized! [chuckling] So energized!

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:15.740
[Mark]: You can't even fool me! You didn't even take one drink! You didn't even open-- Uh-oh.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:17.340
[Bot blasts off like the little einsteins]

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:19.380
[Mark, relieved]: Oh! I thought he was gonna explode!

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:22.380
I mean, in a way if that was the stuff blasting out of his anus...

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:24.760
...then he probably exploded to some degree.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:28.720
[Job Bot]: Back before the universal credit system, some humans had more money

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:32.100
than they knew what to do with and struggled to find ways to spend it.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:35.440
[Mark]: I don't think that's true...
[Grandpa Bot]: Hello! Human!

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:37.600
[Mark]: Hi.
[Grandpa Bot]: Looks like I got some money to blow.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:42.020
What's good here? Get me...stuff. Whatever's good.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.980
[Mark]: How 'bout some of that? How 'bout a little bit of this?

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.920
This? This?  (he's soooo gonna get diabetes)

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:49.660
This?

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:51.660
I should probably scan these, shouldn't I?

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:55.620
Give me that back.
[Grandpa Bot]: Oh, yes, now, that's cool.

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:57.500
How about a couple more things?
[Mark]: Okay, you got it.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:02.860
I'm in it! I'm with it! I'm gonna give you everything you ever wanted! You're gonna be delighted

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:10.280
at all the burritos 'n shit 'n all the grandeur and all the cool jazz and whatever the hell this is.

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:13.400
Dapple Spracks?! It's got what plants crave!( AGAIN!!!!!!!!!!!)

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:15.680
I didn't even scan it! That one's a freebie.

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:19.940
All right, goodbye.
[Grandpa Bot]: All right! Here's a bunch of money. Keep the change!

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:23.920
[Mark]: I don't want the change!
[Job Bot]: Nothing like a little retail therapy!

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:27.520
Make sure you grab their money!
[Mark, grumbling to himself]: Ah, dammit. What is this?

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:31.320
[yelling] I want in!
Ooh. Ah! What's in here?

00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:36.380
Ooh! I got all the cheese! I get it! You're so FUNNY!

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:41.600
[yelling] Pants are falling down!
[grumbling] Usually don't even wear pants.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:44.220
[Corporate Bot]: I need you to reload the stuff on the shelves. Well, there you go. You know the drill.

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:47.600
Gum on the gum rack, magazines on the magazine rack, put stuff where it goes. Get it sorted.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:52.500
[Mark]: Wait, what? I don't even-- "Unplugged Entertainment." Is that a porn mag?

00:12:53.680 --> 00:13:00.820
Ah, it's not sexy at all!
[disappointed grunts as he throws gum at the gum rack]

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.140
Eh.. Ehhh

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:09.020
I don't know where this goes! What is this, hot sauce?
[gargling noises]

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:15.160
Okay. What do I do with it now? Supersize it? How do I-- I  don't know where--

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:19.400
Oh, in the cu-- Oh! Oh, that's handy!

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.700
[Corporate Bot, flatly]: Wow. There you go. Taking the box now. See you later.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:26.860
[Mark]: Okay, bye! Have a good one, whoever you are!

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:30.020
You didn't even tell me that you worked here! I'm assuming you just gave me stuff

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:33.440
that was supposed to be here? And you didn't just steal it from some other store and bring it here?

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:35.440
'Cause that would be weird.

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:39.560
Hot dogs, merch, display, bap-boop, bap-beep, bap-boop, bap-beep--

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:45.720
[Homeless Bot, slurring]: Hello. I don't have any money. Is there anything in there I could have? For free?

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:49.000
[Mark]: Absolutely not! Get out! 
[Job Bot]: Hmm. How about those popsicles in the freezer?

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:51.000
[Mark, in disbelief]: What?!
[Job Bot]: If we don't sell those by tomorrow,

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.640
we're going to have to throw them out anyway.
[Mark, stammering]: What are...

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:58.880
Popsicles don't go bad! They're li-iterally sugar! What do you want them to do?!

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:05.360
They've got nothing but-- I-I-I object to this, because these are worth...two dollars?!

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:10.240
For a popsicle, you frickin' thief?! Who's gonna rob us for two dollars?! Good God!

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:18.820
[Homeless Bot]: Oh. I wasn't expecting to actually get something. Um, if you're able to, can I get a bit of change, too?

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:23.420
[Mark]: Why-- Why would I do this?! Why?! That doesn't make any sense! Boss!

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.660
I don't like this! Charging you for it.

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:31.860
[Homeless Bot]: Oh, thanks! You're a real good person!
[Mark]: Shut up! No, I'm not!

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:35.700
[Homeless Bot]: I'll be going now.
[Mark]: I didn't even want to do any of that! Where are you going?!

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:40.000
[Mark]: Are you gonna steal stuff?!
[deep voice]...Wait a minute...

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:45.160
[Homeless Bot]: Hello there, human! Look at this! I've got a coin here for you!

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:49.560
What could I buy for this? Surely...
[Mark]: Noth--

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:51.940
[Homeless Bot]: ... you can give me something!
[Mark]: N-no!

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:56.000
[Job Bot, sighing]: Just give this bot something. Preferably not something especially valuable.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:59.780
[Mark]: You know what? Just to spite you because I like you less, I'm gonna give him the--

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:07.640
I don't even know wh-- Ah! Oh! Ah! Oh!

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:15.080
Look very deeply into this tube. [in-game fireworks]
[Homeless Bot]: Pleasure doing business with you!

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:19.900
[Mark]: I guess that didn't bother him. Well.
[Job Bot]: Yeah! Sometimes, it was necessary to make

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:23.740
special deals with customers like this to assure their repeated patronage.

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:25.760
[Mark]: HOLLA!

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:29.300
Something happened to him over there. I don't know-- Whoa.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:31.300
[Job Bot]: Oh, no! Here comes trouble!
[Mark shrieks]

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:34.480
[Bandit Bot]: Look, see? Today's not your lucky day, pal.
[Mark]: No, apparently not.

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:37.460
[Bandit Bot]: Open the safe, and give me all your cheddar!

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:39.800
[Mark]: All right. Cheddar, it is.

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:43.460
I already connected the dots on this joke.
[Bandit Bot]: I've got to buy a new pair of shoes.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:44.500
Heh

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:47.800
[Mark]: Here you go!
[Bandit Bot]: Later, chump, you'll never catch me!

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:51.280
[Mark]: I'm not gonna try! Why would I try?! I work for--

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:54.680
Okay! Never mind, then! They went past him.
[Job Bot]: Despite dealing almost exclusively

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:59.540
in low-value products, CONVENIENCE STORES were often the targets of robbery.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:06.260
[Mark]: Uh, am I supposed to feel sad about that? Okay. Anyway. Next customer! Boink!

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:09.940
[Stoner Bot]: I, uh, I want to get some food?

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:14.520
[Job Bot]: I think this bot's had a little too much juice!

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:22.900
Better throw something to get its attention.
[Mark]: Yeah, too much "juuuice." Too much 420 blaze it--

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:28.300
Well, shit. 420 blaze it juice.
[Stoner Bot, startled]: Oh! Uh, hey.

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:32.660
I, um... Oh, I forgot what I want.

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:37.680
[Mark]: You want a burrito. I know this because it says "Burrito Troubles." There you go.

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:42.000
[Stoner Bot]: Oh, this burrito's good!
[Mark]: Yeah! Yeah.

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.000
[Stoner Bot]: Wait. Wait-wait-wait-wait-wait-wait... Wait-wait-wait-wait-wait-wait!

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:49.560
[Mark]: Oh, shit.
[Stoner Bot]: I want, like...like, a *big* burrito. Like *real* big!

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:55.540
[Mark]: Ah, fuck! I gotcha. Don't--stop getting in the way, you asshole!

00:16:55.540 --> 00:17:00.480
Okay, I know what you want: Me to use my magic machine to make this magically--

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:02.480
This is de-- oh, shit.
[Stoner Bot laughs]

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:05.520
[Mark]: You get half of it. Split it even.
[Stoner Bot]: That's what I'm talking about!

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:10.600
[Mark, mockingly]: Yeah, man!
[Stoner Bot, slurring]: Heeeeeeeeeere's your moneeeeeey...

00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:12.600
[Mark]: Why are you saying it so weird?
[Job Bot]: Don't forget to put the cash in the register...

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:17.660
[Mark, to bot customer]: How high are you?
[Job Bot]: ...just because your customer isn't [unintelligible].

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:19.660
[Mark]: Bye.
[Stoner Bot, slurring]: Later...

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:24.060
[Mark]: Bye! Have a good day! [blows kisses] I love you!

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:27.680
[Job Bot]: I haven't seen a mess this big since THE HUMAN UPRISING OF 2027.

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:29.480
[Mark]: Oh, shit.
[Job Bot]: Hold on there, human!

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:32.320
I have just the thing!
[Mark]: What i--

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:36.020
[Job Bot]: Why don't you try it out? The keyhole is right there by the dial.

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:42.780
[Mark]: Oh! I did it! Look at me!
[Job Bot]: This microbot is designed to clean

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:45.280
even the most disgusting human messes.
[Mark making noises, feigning fascination]

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:48.220
[Job Bot]: Grab the controller and clean those stains around the store.

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:56.740
[Mark]: Oh. That is hilarious. [singing] I'm playing a game within a game...

00:17:56.740 --> 00:17:58.500
[Job Bot]: That's enough for now, I think.
[Mark]: Oh, God.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:01.860
[Job Bot]: Just pull the key out to deactivate the robot, and we'll move on to our next customer.

00:18:01.860 --> 00:18:05.060
[Mark]: Oh, man, I have made quite a mess around here.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:08.960
All right, whatever. You're done! Good enough! Supersize that. [Is Mark gonna supersize everything?]

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:13.100
Good key! That's a nice key.
Boink!

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:17.140
What else? Come on! I'm ready! Come on!

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:24.180
Whoa, hello. Uh...
[Clearly Three Children Bot]: Oh, hello! I'm an adult robot!
[Uh-huh, sure you are.]

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:29.900
And I'd like to purchase some fireworks! 'Cause I'm an adult!

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:30.880
[You tryin' to kiss em' mark?]

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:35.880
[Job Bot]: Something about this seems a little bit strange. You should probably check their ID.

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:44.080
[Clearly Three Children Bot]: Oh, yeah! ID! No problem! We--I mean I got that right here!

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:47.820
[Mark]: If it says McLovin, I'm gonna be super pissed!
[Job Bot]: Check it out with your universal scanning device, human.

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:53.620
[Mark]: "Adult Bot," "old enough," "totally legit," "Experi--Expired: Never." I knew what that means.

00:18:54.060 --> 00:19:01.100
I think you're good in my book. Have some of that. Have some of these. Have a good day.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:05.820
Why do these light as soon as I touch them? It doesn't seem like what it's supposed to be doing.

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:07.440
Oh.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:14.000
[Clearly Three Children Bot]: Uh, um, no, wait. That's the wrong one. Try...try this one.

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:18.740
[Mark]: Uh...uh, okay.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:21.940
[Job Bot]: Well, the technology is never wrong.
[Mark]: Okay.

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:27.120
[Job Bot]: That appears to be one legitimately adult robot! I guess you can give them their fireworks.

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:32.140
[Mark]: You got it. It kinda all ran out, but either way, I guess this is okay.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:36.840
Oh, shit. Didn't mean to do that, but here you go.
Ah, shit. There you go.

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:38.840
[Child #1]: Oh, I am totally going to get away with doing this--
[Child #2]: Shut up, dude!

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.960
[Child #1]: All right!
[Mark laughs] Bam!

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:44.120
[Child #1]: Oh, no! Let's book it!
[Mark]: You get out of here, kids!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.420
[2 child bots screaming off into the distance]
[Bot #3]: I can't go back to jail!

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:48.400
[Mark]: You're lucky it's out.

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:53.500
[Job Bot]: That was strange. But the most important thing is that the product is safe. Let's move on!

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:59.240
[Mark]: How does that work?! How does it magically regrow? Are you going to explain that to me?

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:03.620
Boink! All right then.
Well, this seems dangerous. Huh.

00:20:03.620 --> 00:20:08.180
[Cop Bot]: Good evening, human. I understand you were held at bananapoint earlier this evening.

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:11.100
[Mark]: No.
[Cop Bot]: We've captured the suspect. We just need you

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:13.100
to point out who did it.
[Mark]: I ain't no snitch!

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:17.380
[Cop Bot]: Who took your cheddar? Let me make it simple for you. Here are the three suspects.

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:19.920
Just hand me the one who did it.
[Mark]: Oh!

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:21.920
[Cop Bot]: Make sure you're certain.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:24.740
[Mark]: Huh.

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:26.940
Ah.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:30.960
[laughs] "Previous offenses: None."

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:39.800
Uh...yeah, it was this one. This asshole right here! You're fine in my book.
[Cop Bot]: This is the guy who did it? Well, let's go, bots.

00:20:40.140 --> 00:20:44.560
[Cop Bot #2]: Yeah, brah. So I'm going to an area with, like, bad reception.[bruh]

00:20:44.920 --> 00:20:48.620
[Mark]: Okay, bye! Have a nice day, bandito! You're gonna be totally fine...

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:50.360
[Job Bot]: Looks like you're getting the hang of this clerk job, kid!

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:52.900
[Mark]: I sure am.
[Job Bot]: Well, you know how to get back

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:56.780
to the museum if you want to. I'll just be hanging out here while you do whatever you want.

00:20:56.780 --> 00:21:01.360
[Mark]: I'm just gonna chug this pink stuff because it feels good when it touches my brain!

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:03.960
[Mark making unintelligible gulping noises]

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:08.180
Okay! Anyway. Time to eat a burrito and forget all my troubles in another reality.

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:10.980
[Mark making animalistic eating noises]

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:13.660
[Mark shrieking]: Ah! I disintegrated! [Sinefield Ending Song]

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:18.520
Okay. So that is the store clerk job simulator. There's only one left to go, and I've already

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:22.520
done half of it, but I'm gonna blast through it for you guys in the next video that we do

00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:26.460
of this virtual reality stuff. Check out all the other cool stuff, even Oculus Rift stuff that I played

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:30.540
a long time ago. There's links in the description. The playlist: Full of cool videos that you

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:36.320
want to see. Thanks again, everybody, and as always, I will see you in the next video. Buh-bye!

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:38.320
[Subtitles by PikaGuy]

